Subject: [PATCH 6/6] arm64: uapi: key __BITS_PER_LONG on __LP64__

Building LineageOS 16.0 stops in the 32-bit half of the display HAL:

    libhdmi/hdmi.cpp:188:42: error: format specifies type 'ssize_t' (aka 'int')
        but the argument has type 'ssize_t' (aka 'long') [-Werror,-Wformat]

Two ssize_t in one compile. The cause is in how the kernel headers reach it.
LineageOS's generated_kernel_includes (vendor/lineage/build/soong/Android.bp)
runs `headers_install` once, with ARCH=$(KERNEL_ARCH) -- arm64 -- and exports
usr/include wholesale, asm/ included, as -I. That puts it ahead of bionic's
-isystem bionic/libc/kernel/uapi/asm-arm, so 32-bit code picks up arm64's
asm/bitsperlong.h, whose unconditional __BITS_PER_LONG 64 makes
asm-generic/posix_types.h choose `typedef __kernel_long_t __kernel_ssize_t`.

There is no knob in the LineageOS side to make that export ABI-aware, and a
change there would be lost on every repo sync. Fixing the header itself is
smaller and correct for both ABIs: GCC and clang define __LP64__ for LP64
targets only.

Not a backport: Google's deprecated/android-3.10 and LineageOS's msm8996 kernel
both still carry the unconditional definition. The kernel's own build is
unaffected, since it always compiles as LP64.

Found by reading the compile's import_includes file -- part of the include path
is pulled in from there with $(cat ...), so it does not appear on the command
line -- after two guesses about the include order turned out wrong.
---
diff --git arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/bitsperlong.h arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/bitsperlong.h
index fce9c292..ff5ef467 100644
--- arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/bitsperlong.h
+++ arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/bitsperlong.h
@@ -16,7 +16,17 @@
 #ifndef __ASM_BITSPERLONG_H
 #define __ASM_BITSPERLONG_H
 
+/*
+ * These headers are exported once, for arm64, and the Android build hands the same
+ * copy to its 32-bit compiles too. An unconditional 64 then makes ssize_t a long in
+ * 32-bit code. __LP64__ is defined by GCC and clang for LP64 targets only, so key the
+ * width on that and the header is right for both ABIs.
+ */
+#ifdef __LP64__
 #define __BITS_PER_LONG 64
+#else
+#define __BITS_PER_LONG 32
+#endif
 
 #include <asm-generic/bitsperlong.h>
 
